{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Initialize the SDK and track events.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Core Functionality","generated":true,"anchor":"Core-Functionality","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Identifying","doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Tracking","doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/URLSchemeConfiguring","doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/AnchoredTooltips","doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/PushNotifications","doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Initializing-the-SDK","text":"Initializing the SDK","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An instance of the Appcues iOS SDK (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") should be initialized when your app launches. A lifecycle method such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application(_:didFinishLaunchingWithOptions:)"},{"text":" would be a common location:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["func application(_ application: UIApplication, didFinishLaunchingWithOptions launchOptions: [UIApplication.LaunchOptionsKey: Any]?) -> Bool {","  let appcuesConfig = Appcues.Config(","    accountID: <#APPCUES_ACCOUNT_ID#>,","    applicationID: <#APPCUES_APPLICATION_ID#>)","    ","  appcues = Appcues(config: appcuesConfig)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/Config","type":"reference"},{"text":" object has a number of properties that may optionally be set to customize the behavior of the SDK.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Initializing the SDK requires you to provide two values, an Appcues account ID, and an Appcues mobile application ID. These values can be obtained from your "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/studio.appcues.com\/settings\/account","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Managing-Users","text":"Managing Users","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In order to target content to the right users at the right time, you need to identify users and send Appcues data about them. A user is identified with a unique ID."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/identify(userID:properties:)","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For more detail about session management and anonymous user tracking, refer to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Identifying","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Tracking-Screens-and-Events","text":"Tracking Screens and Events","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Events are the “actions” your users take in your application, which can be anything from clicking a certain button to viewing a specific screen. Once you’ve installed and initialized the Appcues iOS SDK, you can start tracking screens and events using the following methods:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/track(name:properties:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/screen(title:properties:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"ty